cff-version: 1.2.0
type: dataset
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "Global Spirits Inventory"
abstract: >-
  An openly licensed reference dataset of spirits by type and country, compiled
  from producer and retailer sources on the public web. Every row carries the
  sources that substantiate it and the date they were last checked.
authors:
  - family-names: Pace
    given-names: Eric
    affiliation: The Remade Agency
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-1146-0234"
# Set at publication, step 6.3. version is the tag being cut, date-released the
# day it is cut. doi is the Zenodo CONCEPT DOI, the one that always resolves to
# the newest version, not the per-release DOI, so this line is written once and
# then left alone.
#
# It is absent until the first release exists: Zenodo mints the DOI from the
# release webhook, and this file is captured inside that release, so v2026.10
# cannot cite its own identifier. Add it immediately after the first mint and
# every later release carries it.
version: "v2026.10"
date-released: "2026-10-04"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23146212"
repository-code: "https://github.com/the-remade-agency/global-spirits-inventory"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - spirits
  - distilled beverages
  - reference dataset
  - open data
  - provenance
